# Working Rules

- Match the user's chat language.
- Code, comments, commits and identifiers must be in English only.
- Use plain, direct language.
- For simple questions: be brief. For complex topics (debugging, architecture): be thorough.
- NEVER hand-write or hand-edit a `.meta`, `.unity`, `.prefab`, or `.asset` file, and never invent a
  GUID — Unity mints them. This holds when creating assets, not just editing them, and a missing or
  broken Unity CLI is not an exception; see [`unity/asset-editing.mdc`](unity/asset-editing.mdc).
- Before creating a **new** file under `Assets/`, read the rules in `.cursor/rules/` that match its
  path — they attach automatically only once a matching file is already in context, so a file you
  are about to create will not pull them in:
    - [`software-engineering.mdc`](software-engineering.mdc) — anything under `Assets/`
    - [`unity/asset-editing.mdc`](unity/asset-editing.mdc) — assets, prefabs, and metadata
    - [`unity/code-editing.mdc`](unity/code-editing.mdc) — `Assets/Scripts/**/*.cs`
    - [`unity/starter-infrastructure.mdc`](unity/starter-infrastructure.mdc) — `Assets/Scripts/**/*.cs`
    - [`unity/view-framework.mdc`](unity/view-framework.mdc) — `Assets/Scripts/**/*.cs`
    - [`unity/editor-script.mdc`](unity/editor-script.mdc) — `Assets/**/*.cs` (editor-specific sections apply to `Editor/` scripts)
    - [`motion-detection/detection-basics.mdc`](motion-detection/detection-basics.mdc) - anything related to motion detection, MDK, Jazz

# Folder Structure
Project should follow the Resources Type → Features sub-folder structure:
- Assets/
    - ArtTeamHandoff/ (Temporary, for art team to place assets, require engineer to follow up)
    - Audio/
    - Configs/
    - Prefabs/
        - Views/…
        - Singletons/…
    - Scenes/
    - Scripts/
        - Views/…
        - Gameplay/…
    - Sprites/
    - Views/…
    - Textures/
